------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web source reproduced — data, composition, states, i18n)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources: useEnergyStats + useVehicles + useUnits + useTranslation bound via the P1/S8
  shared state-holder seam (EnergyStatsSource -> EnergyStatsUpdate -> EnergyStatsModel).
  No HTTP in the view. Mirrors the LifetimeStatsWidget (0055) state-holder pattern.
- Composition: daily-usage area chart (energy series) above a responsive stat grid:
  Total Used / Total Charged (kWh, formatEnergy precision 1) + Avg Efficiency (Wh/km|Wh/mi via
  toEfficiencyDisplay *1000 | *1609.344) + CO2 Saved (kg). Wide (cols>=3) appends Total Cost ($)
  + Net Energy (charged-used, kWh). Compact (cols<=1) shows the big total-kWh number
  (total_wh/1000, 0 dp) + unit caption. isCompact=cols<=1, isWide=cols>=3 reproduced.
- fmtNumber / formatEnergy / convertEnergyFromSI parity reproduced VERBATIM (EnergyStatsFormat,
  locale-aware, halfExpand rounding). Pinned by the runtime harness below (e.g. 0.165 Wh/m ->
  "165.0 Wh/km" and "265.5 Wh/mi"; 345_600 Wh -> "345.6 kWh"; compact 345_600 -> "346").
- Chart: web plots raw `energy_wh` yet labels the axis/tooltip/series "kWh". This surface converts
  energy_wh -> kWh at the display boundary (documented in EnergyStatsWidget.Adapter.swift) so the
  chart + tooltip read correctly — matching the web "kWh" labels, the SI display-boundary rule, and
  the SolarProductionWidget (0093) sibling. NO SILENT DRIFT: the single deviation is documented.
- States (all rendered): loading (skeleton chrome), empty ("No energy data available"), error
  (retry affordance), content; plus stale (amber freshness chip + "values may be stale" banner +
  auto-refresh) and offline (muted chip + "last known energy" banner, cached values kept visible).
  Chart is shown only when daily_breakdown is non-empty (web `hasChartData`); the stat grid always
  shows.
- i18n: all 10 source keys (title/totalUsed/totalCharged/avgEfficiency/co2Saved/totalCost/
  netBalance/noData/dailyUsage/energyKwh) resolve via the widget.energyStats.* table, plus native
  chrome keys (freshness, retry, banners, chart, a11y). Cross-checked: every key used in code is
  declared in EnergyStatsWidget.strings. NO English string literals in native code.
- Accessibility: combined VoiceOver labels on every stat tile, the freshness chip, the chart
  (label + spoken summary "Daily Usage. N days. Peak X.XX kWh"), refresh/open buttons; Dynamic Type
  via Font.TS system fonts; Reduce Motion honored (TSSkeleton shimmer + chart animation gated).
- Telemetry (P1/S11): emits view.opened with surface slug "EnergyStatsWidget" once on appear
  (OSLogEnergyStatsTelemetry -> shared Telemetry.screenView at the composition root).

