BLOCKER ANALYSIS (why the scheme build/test is BLOCKED — pre-existing + out of scope)
------------------------------------------------------------
(a) Shared.xcframework absent. apps/apple/Frameworks/Shared.xcframework is a required build input
    (ADR-004) produced by Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh (the KMP/Kotlin-Native core via
    Gradle, wired as the scheme pre-action). It is not staged in this workspace; building it is a
    separate, heavyweight provisioning step outside this surface's allowed files
    (apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/EnergyStatsWidget.* + this log).

(b) Sibling redeclarations. The TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets group (compiled wholesale into BOTH app
    targets per project.yml) currently contains 14 parallel-slot bundles that each declare the
    shared grid primitives `DashboardWidgetSize` / `DashboardWidgetRegistration`. Compiling any two
    together already fails — demonstrated directly with the toolchain on two UNRELATED siblings:
      $ swiftc -typecheck MQTTStatusWidget.Model.swift UptimeMonitorWidget.Model.swift
      error: invalid redeclaration of 'DashboardWidgetSize'
      error: 'DashboardWidgetSize' is ambiguous for type lookup in this context
    These per-bundle primitives are deduplicated at integration time (the established convention —
    e.g. the 0010 BatteryCellsWidget bundle's *Registry.swift likewise declares them). This surface
    follows that convention (EnergyStatsWidget.Registry.swift) so it compiles standalone; it neither
    causes nor can resolve the aggregate conflict (which exists with or without this surface).

Neither blocker is fixable from this surface's allowed file set, and neither reflects a defect in
EnergyStatsWidget. No green result is being claimed for the scheme build/test (no red-as-green).

